    "classification_notes": [
      "Sites reproduce Note 4 reporting. Merian, Yanacocha and other sites without a separately disclosed minor by-product line carry filed site sales and CAS in the gold line. The consolidated costs applicable to sales measure includes $399m of smaller by-product credits already netted under GAAP.",
      "Gold units are troy ounces. Copper, lead and zinc use metric tonnes. Peñasquito silver uses troy ounces. The issuer reports site CAS per physical unit for co-product metals, which can differ from the quotient of rounded dollar costs and displayed sales volumes.",
      "Filed Note 4 segment capex and MD&A split are on an accrual basis and include capitalized interest. Noncash adjustments and hedge effects are consolidated and unallocated by site. Historical attributable capex totals in the earnings release and forward capital guidance exclude capitalized interest.",
      "NGM reflects Newmont's 38.5% interest and Red Chris reflects its 70% interest by proportionate consolidation. Merian sales and costs are fully consolidated. The consolidated operating costs exclude direct operating expenses of equity-accounted Pueblo Viejo and Lundin Gold."
    ]
